  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member writing a post, I want the formatting bar to be large enough and to follow my density and text-size settings, to offer `[url]` in both forms, and to show distinct icons for \"insert an image tag\" and \"upload an image\". Part of #592 under umbrella #414 (LOT-174, M4). Operator decisions, 2026-11-07.\n\n### Scope (from the analysis on #592)\n1. **Size.**\n   - `FormattingToolbar.swift` uses a fixed 44 pt cell (`:47`) and a fixed 24 pt swatch (`:35`), and never reads `listDensity`.\n   - New cell height: **48 pt in regular density, 40 pt in compact** (operator), scaled with `textScale` (LOT-169).\n   - Swatch and glyph scale proportionally.\n2. **`[url]` in both forms.**\n   - Legacy `HFRTextView.m:205-262` @ 2440d79 offered `[url=XXX]…[/url]` and `[url]XXX[/url]` when nothing was selected.\n   - Restore the choice, and keep today's selection + clipboard path.\n   - HFR renders both (HFR-PROTOCOL, BBCode round trip).\n3. **Icons.** The top upload button and the bottom `[img]` tag both use `photo`. Use `photo.badge.plus` for the top upload button; the bottom tag keeps `photo`.\n4. **Docs.**\n   - Move the LOT-174 row in `docs/LOTS.md` to M4 and update its deliverable; regenerate `tooling/roadmap/lots.json` and `milestones.json` with the documented script.\n   - Update the LOT-174 spec stub, the GAP rows, and CHANGELOG-LEGACY.\n\n### Tests\n- The size rule: density × text scale → height.\n- The `[url]` insertion: both forms, with and without a selection.\n- Each test is shown to fail without the change.\n\n### Mac check\n- iPhone, compact and regular density, smallest and largest text sizes.\n- Both URL forms.\n- Icons in light and dark.\n\nRouting: Sonnet 5.5 writes, Opus 5.5 reviews. Claimed for `ext/francoisgn-composer-a`.",
